    "result": "I fixed `Broken` in `links.go`, but I could not run any tests. The permission prompts blocked `go test` and every other shell command.\n\n**Cause:** all the goroutines appended to one shared `broken` slice with no lock. When two appends happen at the same time, one of them is lost, which is why big sites gave shorter answers.\n\n**Fix:** the goroutines no longer share anything they write. I added a `failed []bool` with one slot per link, and each goroutine writes only the slots for its own chunk. After `wg.Wait()`, one loop collects the failing links in the order you gave them. The chunking is unchanged, so it still uses the given number of goroutines.\n\nI also wrote a test file, `links_tmp_test.go`, and could not delete it. It checks 100,000 links with 16 goroutines, five runs in a row. To check the fix, run `go test -race ./...`, then delete that file.",
